      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomaston%2C_Maine"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A trading post appeared on the St. George River in 1630, marking the first European presence in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomaston%2C_Maine"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town officially incorporated in 1777, becoming a formal municipality after the War of Independence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thomastonmaine.gov/historythomaston"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Knox and Lincoln Railroad once ran through Thomaston, ferrying freight and tourists along the coast.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
